Z||000010||rockcrawl||09-10-2000||10:07 PM||||OK, I'm kinda in the midle somewhere. I like red. I like Yellow. Red <B>and</B> yellow are OK if you want your car to look like a chicken or something. Personally I don't like it. The coffee can tips, I just don't see the point there, no performance gain, and do they really look good? I don't think so. On the other hand, I've had an '87 GT that was lowered to the point of constant bottoming out, with a corvette emblem on the nose, and offset "racing" stripes going over the top.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87gt_1.jpg"> <P>To each his own, isn't that how it goes? I just think some people are taking the rice thing a little too far. No flames guys, we all have an opinion.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
