Z||000016||contra||09-11-2000||07:47 PM||||actually<BR>i hope i dont get called a ricer because i want to put strobe sequentials on my turn signals. I didn't get the idea from any ricers or any fads or what not. i just remember pace cars having those kinds of lights, and i wouldn't mind doing my turn signals like that. i just gotta figure out where to buy strobes for cars :/<BR>heh<BR>call me what you like, but i think it'll look pretty neat, along with my flush headlight system i'm building right now||||reg||1
Z||000017||Greg Piet||09-11-2000||08:05 PM||||As some of you may remember I was involved in a sequential turn signal thread...  it is in my Fiero, and I have stickers on my car too!!!  Does that make me a riceboy?<P>Now these stickers are not for horsepower, but so the flagmen at the track can ID me.<P>I do not think I am really riced out, but I have been joking (I am emphasizing JOKING) with my frined that I should get about 20 non operatonal exhaust tips and line up the whole back of the car with them, since if I put a coffee can on it, they would drag on the ground continually.<P>I think the coffee can is one of the defining marks of a ricecar... A 1 inch exhaust system with a 4 inch exhaust tip performance does not make!<P>As far as what goes with red, I am partial to black...  But then again I want to paint my car orange so what the heck do I know!||||reg||1
Z||000018||Pontiaddict||09-11-2000||09:44 PM||||Someone needs to come up with a rice spotters handbook. People here have been inaccurately claiming that this and that is rice when in fact it is something else.<P>If you really want 2 colors that set each other off try red with really bright blue. Just use the blue on small trim pieces and when your eyes try to adjust to both colors, the blue looks like it is set 6 inches back into the paint. If you do it right, it will cause seizures. (kidding even though it's probably true)||||reg||1
Z||000019||gixxer||09-11-2000||10:53 PM||||Awhile back when I had a CRX, I was on a CRX forum (surprise), and we had a heated debate as to what was and what wasn't,"rice".<BR>Generally speaking, it was agreed (now this was among the phat Honda boyees), that "rice" was equipment on your car that gave it the illusion of being fast. But in fact, this same equipment could actually HURT the performance of the car in day-to-day, or, track use. <BR>Of course, the people that put this stuff on their car would never participate in a race event anyway. <BR>This included ground effects kits, stick on hood pins, fire extinguishers on the A-pillars, lowering it onto the bumpstops, Neuspeed/Type R/Touring Car decals,etc.<BR>My favorite gripe was the stupid non-functional wings(especially for hatchbacks), but I was alone on that one.<BR>No one cared what color(s) you painted your car. If you decided to post a picture of it on the forum and got laughed at to the end of time, that was a risk you took, but in the end, everybody knew it was simply a matter of taste.   <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||MikeSchaefer||09-11-2000||11:26 PM||||Here is the "official" Rice-Spotter's guide: <A HREF="http://www.riceboypage.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.riceboypage.com/</A> <BR>I enjoy it to no end, you will too I promise, (unless you are the guy with the type R sticker, that's just sad man)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.riceboypage.com/shame/hall_of_shame_6/showoff_integra_rear.jpg">  Oh yeah baby!!!!!  Show that bad boy off!!!! :P<BR>Michael Schaefer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/toyotafiero.gif"> <BR>||||reg||3
Z||000021||webbee||09-11-2000||11:59 PM||||LOL...riceboy.com Thanks for that url! I'm still grining!||||reg||1
Z||000022||gtsonly||09-14-2000||07:44 PM||||I see all of us seem to have our own definition of what a "ricer" is. And it seems most of us admit to seeing others driving "riced up" fiero's. It is kind of funny to see people take so much offense to someone on the forum referring to the suspension on fiero's as chevette or citation parts (which they are, just used on the fiero) but yet when a fiero is distorted to look like am import, those same people relish in the thought of creativity. I am not out to bash anyone and I am not picking on anyones car because i do like the looks of customizing but I feel we all can go a tad to far. I just think sometimes we get a little to heavy into oueselves and our cars and we all tend to be very critical at minor things. <BR>  Keep on Truck'in!!!!  That's a joke!<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPS<BR>http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/ubbmisc.cgi||||reg||14
